# Mexican Smoked Salmon Rolls

Inspired by Mexico City’s sushi fusion scene, particularly Sinaloan-style “culichi” sushi

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] [Smoked salmon]{ ing="smoked-salmon" } (cold-smoked preferred)
- [ ] [Ripe avocado]{ ing="ripe-avocado" }
- [ ] [Cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, julienned
- [ ] [Pickled jalapeño slices]{ ing="pickled-jalape-o-slices" }
- [ ] Fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }
- [ ] [Queso fresco]{ ing="queso-fresco" } (optional crumbled topping)
- [ ] [Sushi rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" }
- [ ] [Nori]{ ing="nori" }

### Chipotle-Soy Sauce

- [ ] 2 Tbsp [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [chipotle powder]{ ing="chipotle-powder" } or 1 tsp minced chipotle in adobo
- [ ] 1 tsp [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [honey or agave syrup]{ ing="honey-or-agave-syrup" } (optional)

## Recipe

1. Make the chipotle-[soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" } by mixing all ingredients
1. Prepare [sushi rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" } and let cool
1. Cut [nori]{ ing="nori" } sheets in half
1. Spread [rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" } over [nori]{ ing="nori" }, flip so rice side is down
1. Add [smoked salmon]{ ing="smoked-salmon" }, [avocado]{ ing="ripe-avocado" } [slices]{ ing="pickled-jalape-o-slices" }, [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" } strips, and jalapeño
1. Roll tightly and [slice]{ ing="pickled-jalape-o-slices" } into pieces
1. Top with fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" } and crumbled [queso fresco]{ ing="queso-fresco" } (optional)
1. Serve with chipotle-[soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }

## Notes

1. Chipotle-soy sauce provides the smoky-spicy element characteristic of Mexican sushi
1. Avocado replaces cream cheese as the creamy element
1. Pickled jalapeño adds authentic Mexican heat without being overwhelming
1. Queso fresco is lighter than cream cheese but adds a salty, creamy finish
1. Lime is essential - squeeze fresh lime over the rolls before eating
1. This captures Mexico City’s fusion flavors without relying on heavy cream cheese
